<title>PERU: Peru says May oil output up 3.2 pct vs yr ago.</title>
<headline>Peru says May oil output up 3.2 pct vs yr ago.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru produced an average of 123,220 barrels per day (bpd) of crude oil in May, up 3.2 percent from the same month last year, the Energy and Mines Ministry said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Output in the first five months rose 3.4 percent to 121,900 bpd, compared with the same period in 1996, the ministry added in its monthly report.</p>
<p>Total oil production in Peru dropped 2.9 percent in 1996 to an average of 118,300 bpd of crude.</p>
<p>U.S.-based firms Occidental Petroleum Corp and Petro-Tech S.A., Argentina's Pluspetrol  and state oil company Petroperu S.A. account for more than 90 percent of Peru's total oil output.</p>
<p>((-- Andrew Cawthorne, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
